  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-22T07:47:33.663Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Seems that when the physbone script starts, it records the length of each child bone. If you try to animate those bone's lengths (by animating their position offset) at any point afterward, the change is disregarded and the script snaps it back into place. Animating rotation works properly.\n\nThis is especially annoying for tongues, which are often animated to \"stretch\" out of a mouth while physbones are enabled. As it stands, the \"length\" of the tongue is recorded and locked when physbone activates.\n\nThis (somewhat surprisingly) did actually work properly with the old dynamic bones.",
